economic development always is a sign of the government ‘s power also authorities even sometimes will show their ability to manage the country and existing problems. because always economic progress provides a desirable condition for growth in all fields. because the financial issue is the first subject in each decision and when a government want to run a new for example building at first they have to evaluate this project in terms of financial conditions and check all resources which can

 supply their  needs then they assess other factors.

on the other hand, sometimes especially in poor countries, concentrating only on financial progress  might prevent them to gain other improvements. because they have limited financial and natural resources. so they have to specify their resources for critical cases such as the health care system.

