66f9a9e0518ab60011f687f6,Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social prblems as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statements?,"When in Rome, do as the Romans do. Similarly, when visiting a foreign country with a different language, not knowing it can lead to serious social and practical challenges. I completely agree with this statement for two main reasons, which I will explain below.

First and foremost, human beings are social creatures, and just as we need food and water, we also need the company of family, friends, and neighbors. Effective communication is crucial to forming connections, and language is the primary medium through which we share thoughts and feelings. To integrate with locals, speaking their language is essential, as without it, one may face serious social difficulties. For instance, if you are in France and do not speak French, you will likely struggle to engage with locals, make friends, or socialize. Not understanding others’ conversations can lead to feelings of exclusion and loneliness. Learning and speaking French, in this case, can help avoid isolation and foster a sense of belonging.

Additionally, there are various practical challenges associated with not knowing the local language, including difficulties in shopping, dining out, or seeking medical assistance in emergencies. Without the local language, even simple tasks such as asking for directions or using public transportation can become overwhelming. For example, when I visited China last year, I found it challenging to navigate since most people did not speak English, and I was unfamiliar with Chinese. Simple tasks like asking for directions became a nightmare. I eventually learned some basic Chinese, which made my experience much easier. For this reason, I support the idea of learning at least some basics of a foreign language, even if one only plans to stay short-term.

In conclusion, while English is widely spoken globally, some countries prioritize their local languages. If we plan to visit such places, it is in our best interest to learn the local language to make life easier for ourselves and to show respect for the local culture.",7.5,8.0,7.0,7.0,8.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,324,ec30c5a3f40e6dc3,
6a09f2a1312e6c0011a3ed5f,Some people say it is more important to plant trees in the open spaces in towns and cities than to build more housing. To what extent do you agree or disagree?,"It is commonly argued that it is essential to plant trees in the green areas in towns and cities rather than housing developments. Personally, I can neither completely agree nor disagree with this view for a variety of reasons. 

I partly agree that expanding green spaces plays a vital role in terms of environmental and health benefits. It is because of the reduction of air pollution, especially carbon emissions caused by many factors such as heavy traffic, industrial activities. Furthermore, many cities without trees are facing massive climate impacts, leaving the local authorities struggling to find effective solutions. In fact, trees act as natural filters in order to diminish the consequences of the “greenhouse effect” and environmental issues. For example, many cities with high tree density are clearly making for a more livable environment.

On the other hand, the necessity of building more housing is undeniable due to the growing population in urban centers. Firstly, more people migrate to cities in search of employment, having opportunities to advance good services, and the demand for accommodation is at an all - time high. Therefore, if city planners do not prioritize residential development, the shortage of housing in cities will lead to unsustainable living conditions. Secondly, lack of housing supplies will increase the standards in order to enhance their cost - living by affording personal expenses. For instance, research shows that poverty is getting more widespread in almost all big cities and capitals, which means citizens have to pay their taxes for governments in order to feed the homeless.

In conclusion, it is widely thought that both planting trees and constructing new housing are essential for urban development. Green areas can help maintain a clean environment for citizens whereas building houses contribute to economic growth. In my opinion, city planners should balance these two needs by building high - rise apartments to save land for public parks.",5.0,5.0,6.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Cities,312,e65013763d3f88b1,
627175bcc8e0bb0019a3f913,"In some countries, there are fewer young people who listen to or play classical music these days. Why is this? Should young people be encouraged to play or perform classical music?","In recent decades, we may have discovered that there are rarer juvenile people who pay attention to classical music and fewer youngsters who want to be music performers. It seems to me that the reason could be advancement of modern professions and I will depict it with relevant convictions in the following paragraphs.",0.5,4.0,4.0,8.0,6.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Art,53,956ea0d53f13c06c,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
6461cf6d96d136001a134c8f,"Some people say that to prevent illness and disease, governments should focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","In this contemporary world, diseases are being increased rapidly and also several new issues are arising. However, there are individuals who opine that environmental pollution and housing issues should be controlled by the government in order to reduce sickness. It is somewhat true in my opinion. In this essay, I will state my clear opinion.

Firstly, the main reasons for environmental issues are the increased number of motor vehicles which emits harmful gas which affects both humans and the surroundings. The department should conduct test for every vehicles and should impose strict fines on the illegal one's. Apart from this, the authorities can also increase the public transport facilities which will reduce the usage of private vehicles on the road which will surely decrease the pollution. An another reason is the burning of unwanted chemicals which damages the respiratory system as well as the ozone layer.",1.5,4.0,4.0,5.0,5.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Health,146,c4cad63e48d69e4b,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
