64f0b9cd96269c00181dcbff,"As the number of cars increases, more money has to be spent on road systems. Some people think the government should pay for this. Others, however, think that the user should pay for the cost. Discuss both views and give your opinio","Due to the increasing number of vehicles, more budget has to be put on roads. It has become a controversial topic whether it is the authorities' responsibility to pay for that or it is the drivers'. Both views will be discussed in this essay.

On the one hand, it can be said that citizens pay taxes and it is not fair to pay for any other thing. It should be the government that handles different cities' developments, such as road systems. To illustrate, Canadians pay 13% tax for everything they buy, thus it should be enough for the needed improvements in any section. Moreover, car owners believe that the cost of maintaining a car and buying fuels like petrol is high enough. So many people cannot afford more than that.

On the other hand, extending road systems and maintaining them costs a huge amount of money, and  users must pay a part of it through tolls. It can be a challenging situation for the related authorities. Facing a lack of budget, the quality of the actions can be affected. What is more, all the citizens pay taxes and many of them do not use the roads. As the government uses the taxpayers' money to provide the budget, it is not fair for them. To illustrate, there is a plethora of  who do not drive a car; hence, a large proportion of their money should not be spent on that. 

To conclude, although the government is responsible for the development of road systems, I subscribe to the view that users have to pay their part; for instance, in some toll gates.",8.0,7.0,7.0,9.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Government,270,fbbe071e76191183,
68556d372969c000112221ec,"Some people say that to prevent illness and disease, governments should focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","Recently, the government should have a huge role to prevent air pollution and other issues might face by residents. Although it is a beneficial that authorities have to prevent serious issues but this does not mean that it is a bad idea to do it.

On one hand, authorities have a great role in the society therefore, there are several benifits allowing governments to reduce air pollution in community. To begin, they have to set rules for not only residents but also for business owners by putting fines and taxes for factories and companies to reduce air pollution as a result to reduce illness and disease like lung cancer, skin cancer, and asthma. For examples, in Europe the government put fines for using plastic bag because throwing it can affect on environment negatively. 

In addition, government should encourage people to use public transportation which assist in reducing air gases that emit from cars which lead to air pollution and causing health issues. This by constructing modern transportation systems that allow citizens to use it instead of using their own vehicles.Moreover, authorities should play a significant role to help solving house problems because it is a essential needs for everybody. people live without house will have financial burden which might affect their life in adverse way. Therefore, government should support families during building their house by giving them low benefit loan to build their houses. 

In my own perspective, I totally agree that government has ability to reduce air pollution and home problems which leads to prevention of health issues. This is achieved by set different policies and encouraging people to buy houses.

In conclusion, it is responsibility of government to protect their residents by set different rules and to reduce varities of health condition that society suffers from. I hope that all authorities in the world to take care about their citizens and protect their community.",4.5,5.0,5.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Health,317,c4cad63e48d69e4b,
6039e5e19bde7e001960db9a,"Some people believe that it is good to share as much information as possible in scientific research, business and the academic world. Others believe that some information is too important or too valuable to be shared freely. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","It is argued by many that information should be shared as much as anyone can in the research field, business and the academic world, while others think that some information should be kept secret as they are too important. In my opinion, it is better to keep the information hidden before an idea is executed successfully. 

We are living in an era where hacking is immensely popular. Being an occupant of this age, if a person comes up with something innovative and try talking to people about the idea for better development, that person could run his own business or accomplish research on a topic just by stealing someone other’s thought. Besides, another possibility could be blackmailing. Since we live in a technologically developed age, threatening others has become a common issue these days. If the information one shares contain any personal data, he might suffer from blackmailing. As a consequence, he might lose all his achievement he got through the endeavour. Therefore, no idea should be shared until the task pertaining to that information is not implemented.

Regarding the argument of keeping information hidden, it is quite risk-free. As no one is sharing their ideas, there no chance of getting stolen and also the risk factors of not being successful are less. Because if one comes up with a new idea, he doesn’t have to face that much competition to survive in the current market. Furthermore, he does not have to be worried about his privacy. Hence, the information must be kept a secret.

To conclude, though there are some benefits of sharing with people such as spreading knowledge, the probability of danger is much higher in this case. Thinking about all the potentially grave dangers and taking the risks into account, information is better to keep in one’s mind rather than sharing with others.",6.5,5.0,6.0,6.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Science,306,5c897d8975c11152,
664cad55409a80001187ae3f,"Some people say that to prevent illness and disease, governments should focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","In today's world, pollution and housing problems significantly impact human health. While some argue that reducing environmental pollution should be the government's primary focus to prevent diseases, others believe that other issues deserve more attention. I contend that harmful substances in food are a more significant health threat than pollution, leading to more severe health issues, including cancer. Therefore, I disagree with the notion that governments should prioritize reducing environmental pollution over other health concerns.

One argument against focusing primarily on environmental pollution is that other health risks, such as food safety, may pose a greater threat. While companies and heavy industries do contaminate streams and rivers, leading to water pollution, many countries mitigate this issue with advanced filtration systems. For example, in Taiwan, 80% of households use domestic water filters, ensuring access to clean drinking water. Additionally, housing problems like overcrowded and poorly organized communities are widespread, but their health impacts are often less severe than those caused by contaminated food. Consequently, while environmental pollution is a concern, it may not warrant the highest priority when compared to other health risks.

In contrast, the presence of carcinogenic additives in food is a growing concern that demands immediate government attention. Research indicates that harmful substances in food products are a leading cause of cancer. For instance, Sudan Red, a dye used in solvents and clothing, is sometimes illicitly added to food to cut costs, leading to severe health issues. Unlike environmental pollutants, harmful food additives are directly and rapidly absorbed by the intestines, posing an immediate threat to health. Therefore, governments should prioritize food safety to protect public health effectively.

In conclusion, while reducing environmental pollution and addressing housing problems are important, the presence of carcinogenic substances in food poses a more immediate and severe threat to public health. Governments should focus more on ensuring food safety to prevent illnesses and diseases. By tackling foodborne health risks, we can better protect public health and reduce the incidence of serious diseases like cancer.",6.0,6.0,6.0,5.0,6.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Health,332,c4cad63e48d69e4b,
644410d308a70b0019a4b249,"Some people say that to prevent illness and disease, governments should focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","The globalized world has become more interconnected than ever before in every way especially illness and disease have become globalized problems. In my opinion, we should focus on these problems with our governments but also we need to realize what we are doing about environmental pollution problems. 

Almost all governments around the World are trying to find better solutions for environmental pollution and housing problems. This is the correct way to prevent illness and disease. Furthermore, at the same time goverments  are avoiding implementation of solved  problems. The best example of this is The Kyoto protocol. There are so many solved problems about environmental pollution in the protocol. But some countries do not implement it even though they accepted it, also some countries have given up protocol. Every government needs protocols like the Kyoto Protocol to solve environmental pollution problems. Moreover, the governments should support the building of liveable houses rather than government buildings. In poor countries, like my own country,  huge government buildings have been built and they are not necessary. Governments should realize that the quality of life is much more important than other problems. People will have a better chance to decrease illness and disease if they solve pollution and housing issues.

Furthermore, people should realize that the quality of their lives is dependent on themselves. If people want a better quality house, they should demand more from their local authorities. For example, people may question how their taxes are spent and they may want different resources such as long term loans for house problems. Also, If people want a higher quality of life, they should keep going to develop their own solution for environmental problems. These solutions may be small but the impact will be huge. For example, recycle, using public transport, respect to nature, walking for short distances. These help to become healthy and also make the environment better. Therefore will have a better chance to prevent illness and disease.

In conclusion, people and their governments or local authorities have to focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems together so they can prevent illness and disease.",5.5,9.0,5.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Health,353,c4cad63e48d69e4b,
68bd54cd2a54180012b92840,"Some people say that to prevent illness and disease, governments should focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","Some argue that the most effective way to prevent illness is by tackling environmental pollution and housing shortages. Whilst I agree that these measures are essential for long-term health, I believe that ensuring access to medical treatment is more urgent for the present.

Reducing pollution and improving housing conditions undoubtedly contribute to public health. Clean air, safe water, and adequate shelter lower the risk of respiratory infections, malnutrition, and other chronic conditions. However, such improvements require enormous financial investment and decades of coordinated effort. For example, even though many countries have introduced stricter environmental regulations, the effects of industrial pollution and climate change continue to threaten human health. Similarly, large-scale housing projects take years to complete and often face political or financial obstacles. Therefore, while these approaches are valuable, they provide benefits mainly in the long term.

In contrast, expanding access to medical care delivers immediate results. By increasing the number of hospitals, clinics, and healthcare professionals, governments can provide faster treatment for those already affected by disease. Universal healthcare schemes, such as those in countries like Sweden or Canada, demonstrate that free or affordable access to doctors and medicine not only improves individual health outcomes but also prevents the spread of communicable diseases. This approach is especially vital during public health crises, such as epidemics, when timely treatment and vaccination can save millions of lives.

In conclusion, reducing pollution and addressing housing shortages are crucial strategies for improving long-term health, but they cannot protect populations quickly enough from present-day illnesses. I firmly believe that expanding access to medical care is the most immediate and effective way to prevent disease while societies continue working on long-term environmental and social reforms.",7.0,7.0,6.0,8.0,6.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Health,280,c4cad63e48d69e4b,
63624dd3b0db9a0018b6f933,Some people say it is more important to plant trees in the open spaces in towns and cities than to build more housing. To what extent do you agree or disagree?,"It is clear that flora and greenery are of significant importance in the urban field.Despite the lack of housing in metropolis and towns,a segment of society is convinced that we should plant greenery in urban spaces rather than building housing blocks.I completely agree with this opinion.The coming paragraphs will highlight my point of view along with relevant examples.

On the one hand,greenery plays a key role in our daily life,because they buffer sound, and oxygen and clean the air of carbon dioxide.Subsequently,people  living in a residential field with greenery can have better health.Moreover,green areas are necessary for downtown ecosystems,since they attract various wildlife ,for example,insects,birds, and bees.In addition,planting trees in cities and towns can bring a number of benefits to people and the environment.On the contrary,living in concrete districts without plants may lower the quality of life.

On the other hand,if government build more houses in open spaces,this will lead to problems like congestion, and the development of concrete jungles.As a result,it will cause unemployment  and increased crime rates.For instance,Canada.The residents are moving to the suburban fields because the city is overcrowded.Hence,I do not support the idea of building houses in the capital.Instead,the government can build housing in rural areas.

In conclusion,I personally believe that green zones facilitate the healthy development of residents both mentally and physically.Therefore,governments should give favour  planting trees rather than building more houses.",7.5,9.0,9.0,8.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Cities,258,e65013763d3f88b1,reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
66481979f23a8f001141f085,"Some people say that to prevent illness and disease, governments should focus more on reducing environmental pollution and housing problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","There is a controversial perspective whether authorities should mainly improve the degradation of environment and accommodation issues in order to reduce illness and disease. Personally, I completely consider myself as an advocate of this conception.

Without a shadow of a doubt, in this day and age, there are abundant problems leading to the increase of illness and disease, yet I suppose governments should concentrate more on environmental matters. And this due to the fact that environmental issues directly influence the living surroundings of people. For example petroleum plastic bags as well as transportation releasing large amounts of carbon footprint may lead to respiratory illness or lung cancer. Additionally, by clearing the tree without permissions for self-serving, dwellers do not have adequate sources of oxygen to live. Thus, making an improvement to environmental issues by the authorities plays such a paramount role in protecting us from illness and disease.

 On the other hand, while the environmental problems are conquered, housing problems also should be enhanced simultaneously by the governments. And the explanation for this could be that catastrophic and contaminated houses with no ventilation are the place where newly negative bacterias are produced. For example, Covid 19 virus which was originally from the Vu Han slum area has taken over millions of lives as the closeness of houses contributing to outbreak of disease. Hence, it is important that housing problems be dealt with immediately by the governments.

 In conclusion, I would contend that to protect individuals from illness and disease, the authorities should mainly concentrate on environmental pollution and housing problems.",5.0,6.0,6.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Health,260,c4cad63e48d69e4b,
