5fc26ce6a3de4a00187662c1,Nowadays people live longer after they retire. How does this affect individuals and society? What can be done about this?,"In today’s world, because of the advancement in the medical sector more and more health conditions are becoming curable, as a result, in general, the death rate of elderly people has decreased and they live longer even after their retirement. In some ways,it has negative impacts on the individuals themselves and  society as a whole especially in case of finance. These problems can be solved by advanced government norms which favours senior citizens.

           Firstly, living for many years may not prove to be enjoyable for the majority of  old people. Since  the retirement pension,they get will not serve any purpose as the amount is not sufficient. Moreover, getting older means the health is deteriorating day-by-day which deprives their physical autonomy. Secondly, this problem in one way affects  society too, because most of the people in their old-age suffer from diseases like arthritis, diabetes or any cardiovascular diseases. Thus, they need advanced treatment techniques to sustain their life. Acting as a chain reaction, for this purpose to fund more in the health sector, authorities will increase the tax which in-turn affects all the other citizens.

          The best fixes of these problems can be achieved by governing bodies by introducing certain norms. For example, in New York City besides the social security benefits, which is barely enough for daily requirements there are certain helpline numbers through which retired elderly people can get access to cheaper daily utilities like grocery and medicine. Additionally, some apartments especially for the senior citizens are also available whose rent is quite affordable for them.

       In conclusion, the drawbacks of living longer after people have stopped working can be easily tackled by forward-thinking governmental policies. It will be beneficial for all the age groups as old-age is a bitter truth of everyone’s life.",9.0,8.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Society,297,d63de09391194cff,
635a2be59f701e0018caae42,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","We are living in a world that study abroad is become more and more prevalent. However, there has many controversial arguments surrounding that living in a foreign country where we can not speak our mother tounge. While some people said it may brings out some social issue such as practical problems.

On the one hand. Studying abroad or being a denizen could make us face with language barrier. It is hard to communicate when we move to new place. Especially foreign country, multilingual communication could lead us to misunderstanding about study and daily life. 

On the other hand. As a result of language conflict, we may suffer the scene of isolation and inferority when contacting with people. The language barrier might make it difficult for us to engage in activities as a way to fitting back society. Not only the difference in language but also in culture. Living in the multicultural neighborhood also lead to serious problem. For example, the descrimination on the ground of race and culture are inevitable.

Overall, I strongly agree with the opinion that living in a country where we have to speak another tounge could be reason for some social and practical problems.",2.5,6.5,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,198,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
61005e12e6772000188b61dd,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","A slew of people's desire to visit a foreign region has been increasing throughout the years. Living in a foreign country, many elucidated social and practical problems they have faced throughout the years. There are compelling reasons in which may have caused the non-native to go through such events. This essay will elaborate on the plausible reason to support what are the reasons along with some relevant examples. 

First of all, the practice and the living style of one nation to another may vary in various ways. To contribute with the culture that is different from one that is not familiar to another may give a big conflict in social and practical problems. For instance, a study has shown there hhaseen an inincreasednumber of depressed international students throughout the world who eventually moved back to their country because they were not able to blend in with the foreigners due to aa lackk of common background and culture. Moreover manybusinessesses that branches overseas have failed and closed down due to different working and social environment between the countries. Therefore nowadays many people try to first study the background before they decide to move to that a certain country. 

In conclusion, globalization may be a new trend thisis being encouraged throughout the world,howeverhowever there are many consequences that come along with it. One should consider and ameliorate to get along with the foreign culture to decrease the possibilities in facing problems by studying and learning their perception and social backgrounds.",3.5,4.0,4.0,5.0,5.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,249,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
633a8563e5ada70018b41189,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems- To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","It is often argued that being a resident of a nation where the individuals have to bilingual May gives the Emerson some antisocial nuisances which can affect the society to a great extent along with some serious issues. I ,however, disagree with this argument and will explore the predicament in this discourse .

The first and foremost reason is that being bilingual can explore the higher studies opportunities along with the better job choices world wide. For instance, the language interpreters jobs now a days are on high demand at the international level as it provides a very good salary or livelihoods. Such work does not demand any high degrees instead once's has to complete any certified course within shorty period of time and can easily earn good payment monthly.

Secondly, it has been observed that learning or communicating in different languages aids intelligence and creativity among the youngsters and teenagers . The great psychologist Dr. Caltrop at Auckland University conducted a survey and mentioned that scholars who communicate in various languages get better chances to learn divesred culture and traditions globally.

Summing up, communicating in diversied languages not affect the local communities instead it plays a significant role to bring the local and internationally bodies more and more close.",3.0,5.5,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,208,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
63e4a30b96e92a00181ad52c,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Nowadays, regarding the development era and fast changes in the world, it can be seen that the amount of immigration is increasing considerably. Consequently, the immigrants have to live abroad and speak a foreign language. I totally agree with the given statement. This essay intends to express my justification.

Firstly, language and the ways of using it to express ideas and communicate with the public, have a close relation with culture. In general, we consider our culture during speaking. As a result, when we have to speak another language from an unfamiliar culture, we experience culture shock. As a consequence, a lot of mistakes are made in our speaking. As a vivid example, the forms of behaviour between family members are different in every country, and if you want to speak about this according to your culture, many problems will create in terms of security and safety.

Secondly, misunderstanding is an inevitable difficulty for this topic. In fact, almost all immigrants are trying to be perfect in a foreign language. However, there are some inevitable restrictions, in spite of their efforts. Therefore, this matter causes many practical difficulties that are related to language. For instance, in a vital condition, the importance of words and verbs is remarkable. There is significant evidence that illustrates the harms of misunderstanding in factories.

To sum up, living abroad and forcing to speak a non-native language have a high potential to cause various kinds of problems. Particularly, in terms of practical issues, it will have noticeable effects more than other fields.",8.5,9.0,9.0,7.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,256,76b004e7631f7335,
65589a60c86bfe0013a5a62d,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Nowadays, an array of masses is living abroad for various reasons. However, they aspect many difficulties  with speaking another speech, and this brings crucial point, whether social or practical. I strongly agree with this notion and in this essay, I will shed light on my viewpoints.

To begin with, the major social problem that occurs due to speech barriers is with making friends, because friendship with local public needs more than just a basic grasp of the native speech. Due to a lack of good communication in foreign languages, public find difficulty in making sound relationships with their neighbours and colleagues, which makes them feel isolated and hence may cause mental problems like depression and anxiety. For instance, immigrants who have difficulty  understanding the English speech feel overwhelmed with English information, are unable to follow any public speech or any group conversation, and seem helpless to understand their cultural values.

In addition, public also confront many practical challenges. One of the major point public aspect is while travelling. Since bus stop signs are written in the native speech,  public with problems in the local speech do not understand where to get off the bus. Besides, immigrants aspect difficulties in healthcare and legal services. Due to weak communication, public find themselves unable to explain their diseases to the doctor or any legal injustice they are facing to their lawyer. For example, in China, all the road signposts are written in the Chinese speech, and the speech they use for official purposes is only Chinese, so immigrants who lack good knowledge of the Chinese speech aspect many practical point.

To conclude, I believe that public encounter many social and practical point in other countries due to less proficiency in the local speech, and the government should provide suitable support to them for tackling such problems.",4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,303,76b004e7631f7335,
62966935349bd000180dd411,Some people say that now is the best time in history to be living. What is your opinion about this? What other time in history would be interesting to live in? Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.,"Many individuals believe that we all are living in the best era in history. I strongly agree with this opinion as our lifestyle is convenient and still getting better due to the advancement of technology. However, sometimes I feel like living in the past  and the reasons will be discussed in this essay.

In today's time, our life has become easier and more comforting due to advancement of the technology. Firstly, travel has become faster and more convenient. For example, back in the era people used to travel through bicycles, animal carts, etc which were slow modes of transportation, and now cars, trains, and aeroplanes have made travel faster than ever in history. Secondly, daily chores have become easier with the help of gadgets and people can now do their work with lesser effort. For instance, dishwashers, vacuum cleaners etc. are now being used to do the daily household chores. Thus, today's era is the best time to live in as technology has invented great things to make our life easier.

However, sometimes I feel like going back in time when life was running at a slow pace which is our ancestor's time. During those days, people were more connected and used to have more fun as they were able to spend more time with their loved ones due to minimal involvement of technology. To exemplify, nowadays individuals connect with loved ones on the phone or video calls whereas earlier they often used to meet each other in person, which increases the feeling of belongingness. That is why earlier times were more happy times as most people were able to spend more quality time with each other.

To conclude, though our lives have become more comforting and convenient with the help of technology,  earlier times were more peaceful and joyful as individuals were more connected with their families as they hardly had any involvement in technology.",8.0,8.0,7.0,7.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,History,316,908b6c3839150b73,
5f0e9927401ea400186c67ee,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","LTo live in a foreign country where a  native language is required to speak can create severe problems both in social and daily life, I completely disagree with this view.

When someone is living in a country and speaking a native language can not cause crucial problems. The First reason is, nowadays students who intend to pursue higher study abroad are bound to fulfill the language requirements; otherwise they will not be qualified to apply in international universities. Hence for having language skill, international students can socialise with students as well as capable of following lectures that reduces the prospects of facing any problems in their lives. On the other hand, immigrants who are going to foreign countries get the opportunity of participating language courses provided by the government. For instance, United Kingdom has been providing English language course for the newly arrived foreigners: where in Germany many universities have taken initiatives of mandatory six months long intensive German language course for the foreign pupils.   

In foreign countries people can face social and practical problems not only for language but for other factors as well. Firstly, students may pass their language tests but if they are not financially affluent or have not secured fully funded scholarships, to cover their living costs and tution fees, will encounter problems to bear their daily expenses and continue their study.Secondly, apart from the cause of language, religion has already created conflicts and polarisation in different spheres of people's life who are living abroad. As in today's modern world religious extremism and conservative views have reached in an alarming state that people have become susceptible in coping with foreigners' and embracing their customs and cultures. In the long run, because of this the social bond in the communities are lessening.

In conclusion, nowadays people are aware of the necessity of language and also acquire skills in foreign language as they plan to live in abroad. Therefore students and immigrants do not face difficulties in a foreign country for the language but mainly for monetary and religious factors.

