A situation where one has to settle in a country that uses a completely new style is a tough one since this foreign accent is not your forte. There would be several issues that one would face while settling in this country, one has to always carry a dictionary to translate their wording into his/her native expression. Working in a country where you’re new to their terminology is an added disadvantage, as one doesn’t fit the basic criteria. Though the practical struggles are endless and what adds up to this list are the social struggle to be accepted by the locals, it is a human tendency to differentiate people based on their lingual preferences. A continuous fight to be socially accepted in that country will be extremely challenging. 
I personally encountered this issue once when I went to a foreign land as a part of my business trip, every point where I wanted to communicate, it was a challenge for me. I carried a dictionary every time be it shopping, commuting, and while carrying out my day-to-day activities. Though globalization has reduced this struggle by introducing English as a prime speech for most of the countries, thus helping people communicate better and connect to a wider audience. English still hasn’t been adopted by most of the countries.
