60e3e71b00657e00180f58c6,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Living abroad is a difficult life style for individuals to choose, and language is the most challenging problem to be solved for those in my opinion.

What I concerned most is that language barrier could most be eliminated by the time floating, communication abilities is an accumulating process taht one needs to pay a lot of efforts to fulfill the task. Secondly, the culture shock is another barrier for those oversea habitants to adapt, they have to obey the conventional rules no matter how they consider it. Thirdly, self-awareness in the new circumstance for them could be doubted by themselves because of the social behaviour and potential pressure.

On the another hand, the acutal living statues related to the mind-set of individuals. Normally, how those oversea habitants could cope with the condition decides the social and practical problems.

Overall, foreigners have always modified to encounter the challenges which might affect the life, however, speaking a foreign language is the way to immerse into the life and culture of the foreign country.",2.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,171,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
5ff600dfdfa82d001816fb55,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Survival of the non-native overseas without the knowledge of the local language creates a barrier in connecting with folks and in performing day to day activities. I completely agree to the statement cited above and this essay will discuss the issues faced by the individual residing in abroad without the command over the native speech.

Firstly, staying at a distant place away from the family and friends has various difficulty including loneliness. To cope up with this issue, people required to be sociable. Connecting with people and finding new friends is the only way to cope up with the issue, which is only possible after having some knowledge of the local wording. Furthermore, lack of communication with the folks and incapability to understand them creates hurdles in getting connected socially. Consequently, which results in mental issues such as anxiety, stress and depression. For instance, recent studies had shown that around 70% of the migrators which were incapable express and to connect with natives were found to be victims of mental illness.

Secondly, unable to speak and understand  foreign people while residing not only cause social troubles but also many practical problems. Particularly, in case of the medical emergency individual must have some basic knowledge local way of communication so to inform the doctor about the exact pain the patient is having so as a doctor can diagnose and treat. For example, one of my friends residing in Denmark had a severe stomach ache for which she consulted the doctor but failed to explain exactly what happened and the medical history of her ache. Subsequently, resulted in getting numerous examinations done and delay in the treatment.

To conclude, in my view, it is practically a serious problem for visitors to survive in a country where everyone uses a foreign way to communicate with each other. Some information and basic requirements of international language must be gained prior to visiting, to avoid physical as well as mental troubles.",9.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,326,76b004e7631f7335,
619bc87db707630019873ba4,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Culture shock refers to the impact of moving from a familiar culture to the one that is unfamiliar. This impact is a term used to describe what happens to people when they encounter unknown complications and a vicious circle. Culture shock is typically divided into some stages, for instance, honeymoon, frustration, adaption and acceptance. Almost everyone is affected by it in one way or another, therefore, it needs to be reconsidered as an issue. When we live in a foreign country we experience confusion, disorientation and anxiety for the reason local people have different values and ways of thinking. As humans we always want to welcome change and come out of comfort zone but when it comes to experience it we fear what the outcome will be. And also your health is might affected and you may get headaches and start worrying about your health more. You can not concentrate enough and as a result find it harder to focus on your life. All these effects causes by the shock of a new environment and people.",2.5,4.0,4.0,5.0,5.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,176,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
64acdffa7484d100184ecb47,Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?,"I agree with this statement because living in a country where I have to speak foreign language needs a lot of preparation, especially for people who find it hard to make friends with others. If you don’t prepare enough, you might get serious social problems. When we move to a country that speaks foreign language, we need to learn the foreign language. Because how can you communicate if you can’t speak the language? 

Language is the first thing you need to prepare before you move to a new country. The second thing you need to prepare is your way to adapt. You need to learn how to adapt. However each person has different ways and different times to adapt. If you are an extroverted person or you love meeting new people, maybe you will adapt and make new friends easily. 

But, if you are an introverted person and you can’t start a conversation, you will find it hard to adapt in a new country and you might take a long time to make friends with others. In my opinion, those two things are the most important things when you want to move to a new country. If you don’t prepare enough, it can cause serious social problems because you can’t communicate without language, and you can’t socialize if you can’t adapt.",3.5,4.0,4.0,6.0,6.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,221,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
5c9bc4b0699f4c86b4801ee1,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement ?","Nowadays people move from one country to other for many reasons such as education, job and tourism. When a person go to a new place where a different language is use by majority, it creates some sort of difficulties. If the person is not able to speak language of a particular place where he lives, definitely create many issues in terms of day to day life and social activities.

Many people experience difficulty to understand foreign language. It create issues in communicating and expressing ideas. When a person live in an abroad country, it’s always good to use language which is using in that country. For example, if a person want to travel to another place, he should be able to speak with others and read the sign boards.

 Sometimes speaking in different language can create friction between communities. There are chances that other people may misinterpret the words which are used by people. For example, there people from many communities live in a small town, so it’s important to respect their social life and attitude too. Speaking foreign language may be difficult for many people. It makes the left miserable for them. It is always important to understand the social background of the people with whom we interact.

To conclude, it is always advisible to speak in the language which is prevalent in the society where ever you live. It help to make the interaction with others and transmission of information in a better way.",3.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,246,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
601e83065319a100180edbca,Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement.,"It is stated that many complications can come when you are having a life outside your home country in terms of speech like communication barrier and daily life obstacles. I firmly agree with this statement, as I myself has suffered through such circumstances. I will further explain in detail why I agree to it and what are the impacts of overseas language on our daily routine.

When you are unknown to a foreign accent, then living there can bring many complications. There are so many people who are living in a country but are totally unaware of its language. For example, when I came to Saudi Arabia, I was totally unfamiliar with there voice. Therefore, the conversation was becoming a huge barrier, when I go out for shopping and ask for anything, salesperson never understands that what I'm trying to tell. So, conversation with local became a complex thing for me.

You can get trouble in getting a job in a country whose native jargon is unknown to you. As the job requires daily contact, consequently a person who is well qualified and much more experienced but lack in communication will get no jobs. For instance, In Canada ,immigration many qualified people fail to get the invitation because of fewer bands in IELTS test. IELTS is an English language proficiency test that is compulsory to get into Canada. Accordingly, learning the jargon of a country where you want to live is essential if you don't want to face issues.

In conclusion, it is said that having a life in a country whose speech is not known to you can affect many interaction issues as well as a dilemma in daily life. I totally agree with this statement, if you are not familiar with there speech than you can not communicate with them. Moreover, you get difficulty in getting any job and you end up with frustration because of not being able to understand what another person is saying.",8.5,7.0,9.0,8.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,328,76b004e7631f7335,
6166fbbcd0e8970018fc6ca5,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Nowadays, people immigrate to other countries for different purposes such as studying or working and embrace all obstacles, pursuing a better life. In many cases, travelers must learn the language of the country they had traveled, which is not English most of the time. Despite the usual difficulties that will come with immigration, learning a whole new language also will engage people with numerous social problems. This essay had been written considering that the writer believes it can be arduous in many aspects to live abroad.

At first, let us take a look at a matter called “cultural differences” and examine the crucial role of the language in it. Basically, all nations in the world had been formed by a combination of components like habits, behaviors, rituals, and last but not least, language. So, what will happen to you as an outsider who is not able to communicate with others by their words?

To start, you cannot handle your initial needs like asking about the nearest supermarket or how to get a ticket for the bus. Subsequently, more complex issues will come one by one. For instance, it is likely impossible for you to communicate with your college friends at a party or have a chat with them about a match that you saw last night; at least not in the way that you wanted to express yourself. And this will make you feel like a total stranger. As a result, lack of suitable skills in language exacerbates all crises you have predicted would come.

In addition, as it has been proved we are all social beings by nature and tend to live with crowd from the beginning of human history. Likewise, if we cannot make friends or fall in love with anybody, our mind starts to collapse very soon. Proof of this, it can be seen in universities that students who have come from other parts of the world are more to get depressed compared to natives or students with similar speech. To illustrate, while people in Scandinavian countries do not have same language, they have fewer obstacles in the way of adaptation because they have similarities in words and grammar which make atmosphere less unfamiliar.",4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,367,76b004e7631f7335,
61f8003240113600180037a0,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement ?","Living outside of the home for those who need to use different languages in daily life leads to significant communication and practical issues. Although it’s acceptable that It can not be a problem for some folk to have a conversation with others, I strongly agree with that idea and it may result in serious problems for migrants although technological developments are improving every day to assist them.

People who immigrate to a foreign country have to speak the local language since one of the necessities for individuals is communication. For example, for expatriates, when they are forced to immigrate to another province to continue their life initially they face a problem that they can not explain themselves accurately. Inhabitants may misunderstand them. Foreigners are supposed to speak a language that they have never spoken before. This may cause for them some documental problems in the immigration office at the beginning. In addition, they might not afford their needs in their daily life because of their poor communication. This state causes serious drawbacks for the community.

On the other hand,  the local people, may become more biased toward them because they don’t understand them. For example, in Turkey, according to my observation, foreigners are misunderstood in many ways. More than three million strangers live in this country and mainstream media controlled by the government shows them offensive. As a result, this creates gaps between local people and evacuees in society. 

In conclusion, as an individual, living outside of home country bring about some  challenges such as social and practical. All in all, governments should take steps for migrants and refugees and authorities may encourage them to take courses to learn local languages to maintain their lives and this is important for  society.",8.0,9.0,6.0,8.0,8.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,291,76b004e7631f7335,
5ed263ad81fb6300181e2069,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement ?","Majority of people believe that living outside your motherland where nobody speaks your primary language can affect your life and on a  daily problems and keeping in touch. I probably agree with this statement and I will give same arguments and examples in the following paragraphs. 

Generally speaking, communication is the main problem we would meet in foreign parts. If we do not know the language, we will face to the trouble get acquainted with foreign people and making new friends. Get in touch with  new people in the new city can be solution of being alone and filling ourselves isolated.

However a great deal of people know English it can make life easier for immigrants to survive the first few weeks in a foreign country. In fact if someone hears new language every day every minute our brain will automatically accustom. And learning a foreign language in a foreign country mach more easier and effective than learning it in our country without any immigrations. Thanks  to our hands and mimics we can show what we wont to speak and show direction with the help of gesture 

To sum up, greater number of people suppose that having to converse in a foreign language can cause problems for immigrants. But, I think this is not a big issue because our brain can adapt easily in the new atmosphere within a few weekends.",4.5,5.0,6.0,5.0,5.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,231,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
61adb9ba42d8aa001946240a,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Staying in a country that doesn't use one's native language can cause severe social problems and practical problems. This is a frequent topic of discussion for second language learners. Although language boundary is one of a cause of the problems, I believe it won't create serious problems in long term.

Foreign language speakers usually have communication problems when they first arrive in a foreign country. The language boundary is obstructed that making one can't blend into a new society. Sometimes, socializing requires advanced language skills, for example, playing jokes and memes. In addition, the boundary can cause misunderstanding of tasks or achievements. Eventually, it will lead to practical problems.

On the other hand, creating serious problems is not depend only on language skills, instead, soft skills play more important roles. Serious social problems will not occur if a speaker speaks with good attention. Body language, gestures, facial expressions are  spontaneous actions of speakers. Its are a major part that a listener uses to evaluate the attention of the speaker. Moreover,  practical problems can be prevented by an experience of working. Many managers use methods, frameworks or tools besides from language skills to prevent misguiding a scope of work. Therefore, there are many ways to prevent the problem without requiring expertise in the language.

To Summarise, insufficient language skills can create social problems and practical problems. However, I disagree that it will lead to serious problems. I believe interpersonal skills play a more important role to create severe problems for each person.",6.5,6.0,6.0,6.0,8.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,251,76b004e7631f7335,
639b01f2543dbe00185216e3,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems,as well as practical problems. To what extend do you agree or disagree with this statement?","In modern times, migration has become overwhelmingly popular because of the increase in the number of people learning another language. However, migrating to a country where someone needs to speak a different language rather than their mother tongue might create social and practical problems. I completely agree with this statement. In this essay, my contention will be further elaborated. 

  To embark, immigrants must be aware that knowing a language does not always bring the ability to familiarise themselves with that language’s culture, and being foreign to the culture might result in social isolation. For example, in Germany, immigrants have the highest rate of social isolation because Germans have various cultural traditions, which need to be learned to attend a social activity. These requirements create many social problems for foreigns. 

   Another outstanding example of why there are many problems with speaking another language is the language barrier. Local dialects establish diversity in a language, and one can only learn several of them if they are not a native speaker. This situation may result in different struggles in daily life. For instance, if an immigrant goes to an urban area, local habitants might understand them differently, which may result in conflicts. 

   In conclusion, life in a country where one speaks a foreign language might have harsh consequences, such as social isolation and conflicts. From my point of view, this statement cannot be submerged in the human mind, so I adopt a similar stance.",6.0,5.5,7.0,7.0,8.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,241,4c6688c89561fba5,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula
5daec770635c680018ccab34,"Some people think that newly built houses should follow the style of the old houses in the local areas, while others think that people should have freedom to build houses of their own styles. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","There is an opinion that all new buildings must be built in one style as existing houses; however, others suppose that all people should have a right to build their own accommodations in according to their own touchstones. In this essay, I am going to discuss both views and give my own opinion on this topic. 

On the one hand, it is very picturesque to see all houses in one style. Firstly, many people live in densely populated areas, for them, this can be very annoying and stressful to see a myriad of houses in different colors, styles or number of storeys. In other words, we would not see such beautiful and tiny streets and buildings in the European cities because if everyone has a right to build as he wants, there would be only skyscrapers because they are very high-yielding for owners. So, the second point is that governments should have some restrictions on the construction. This means that people have to receive government approval in order to build a house in their own style. Finally, in many countries government promote the idea that buildings, and consequently, streets should stay in the same style. For instance, governments have grants so as to support the restoration of old and antique houses, which have been built centuries ago.

On the other hand, owners should have rights to express their personality and build their houses as they want. Firstly, accommodations can be a byword of views on the modern art of owners. For example, they can build astonishing and unimagined dwellings in styles which they like. Secondly, these buildings can bring something new on streets like new colors or design, and consequently, all local areas will have some highlights, peculiarities. Locals can be proud that their neighborhood has some differences from other districts.

To sum up, despite some people arguing that all owners of one area should adhere to a single style, others believe that everyone should be tolerable and has a right to build in their own style. I am inclined to believe that all houses in one area should be in one single style because it is just beautiful when all houses are almost the same. Moreover, other styles would be seen as a fly in the ointment.",5.5,9.0,5.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Housing,378,1c945805324195cf,
64396aef08a70b0019a49f30,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems.To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","New immigrants are often reported as victims of domestic violence in Taiwan, saying that they do not have friends around them to help due to language barriers. From my point of view, I disagree that language disfluency will lead to social isolation or even make one suffer difficulties in daily life.

To begin with, languages are not necessities in connecting with others. Common interests can be found through sharing something which is beyond speech, such as music or paintings. For example, I have a neighbour who is from Vietnam and she always cooks her meal as I prepared mine. The special smell of her exotic dishes spreads through the windows of my house. Once upon a time, I met her outside the garden and asked her for the recipes. This becomes the beginning of our friendship. Thus, it shows that there is some happiness that can be shared without words.

Although some foreigners might get frustrated when they come into a situation that is highly required communication, like describing their illness conditions or explaining the hairstyles they want with accurate words, there are some other workarounds to resolve these problems. For instance, patients who are not fluent in local languages can look up the words in a dictionary in advance. Similarly, foreign customers in hair salons can search for pictures of the particular styles they want to precisely express their needs.

In conclusion, despite some inconveniences in daily life, there are many ways which do not need intimate knowledge of languages to shorten the distances with strangers. After all, what matters is always the friendly attitude behind one's actions.",7.0,8.0,7.0,6.0,6.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,269,76b004e7631f7335,
621d24db63df6c0019055130,Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?,"Many people believe that it can be challenging that speak a foreign language when you live in a country. While living in a different country might have various advantages, I personally agree with the point of view that it can come with serious issues.

First, working or living in another country has lots of benefits. For instance, when a number of employees choose to work in another country, the workplace and country they live in might change due to this situation, and they can work harder to adapt to this environment. When these workers challenge themselves, they can go further in their careers.

However, the language may be the most concern for the dwellers who are not native to it. First and foremost, speaking language and the language which is learned from books are much different from each other. Since these books are designed using the literacy and the formal version of the words and the structure. Furthermore, the books might not also have the metaphorical meaning of the words and the speaking forms with mostly metaphors, adages, and idioms. Therefore, if the language is known, speaking cannot always be understood. It can cause a number of problems for foreign residents. Firstly, finding a new friend may become difficult due to the language barrier. Secondly, handling paperwork can be quite demanding. For example, if the emigrants ought to deal with paperwork for the government for their visa or work permit, the language can be an obstacle for them. Because writing the incorrect word can cause serious issues. Therefore, I believe that non-native speakers might encounter plenty of problems.

To conclude, the dwellers who live in another country need to speak this country's language, and learning a foreign language completely is hard to do. Therefore, they might face some conflicts. As a result, this can be burdensome for them.",7.5,8.0,6.0,6.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,308,76b004e7631f7335,
63496c470869d1001829cb7f,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","In the contemporary epoch, people's tendencies to travel and immigrate has greatlly increased. A high proportion of individuals opine that it causes severe social complexities and practical issues, and that is primarily attributable to communicating with foreign languages. According to my perception, it is an outstanding oppurtunity to live overseas because it enables us to fully learn a new language and encounter various customes. The impending discourse will elucidate the aforementioned topic in the subsequent paragraphs.

To commence with, language barrier is the leading causative factor of this concern. Inhabiting in a new environment, in which people are forced to obtain new language competences may seem unpalatable from some perspectives. That is due to the time-consuming process of getting accustomed to the new ways of interacting with one another. Thus, it eventually causes multitude social problems such as lack of confidence, introversion and occupational disabilities. Consequently, people can not enhance their capabilities and therefor face numberous practical difficulties.

On the contrary, there are myriad reasons to support the merits of speaking with a new toungue. First and foremost, the best way of improving linguistical skills is to constantly communicate with natives. Moreover, getting utterly used to a new tradition becomes feasible in case we live in a region, in which a foreign toungue is utilized. The above-mentioned experience will be an unmitigated joy and satisfaction in terms of being a plateau in that nation's language.

In conclusion, it is rational to assume that living in a country where individuals ought to be fluent at a new language can have lots of perks and demerits. However, the advantages ulitimately outnumber the downsides.",5.0,6.0,6.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,271,76b004e7631f7335,
66d3828d4dcc5a00110de611,It is better to learn the way people lived in past through films and videos records than written documents. To what extent do you agree or disagree?,"i guess it is better to learn the way people lived in past through films and videos records than written documents. it will be more exiting and clear for the viewers to learn. in my opinion i see that filming people who lived in the past more that documents in way much things to inform the people the right way, on the other side some people see the documents and written books better than videos, they see it big proof because the old people wrote it, but in my opinion i see the videos is much better and clearly than documents and easy to share it and explain it",1.5,5.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,History,109,69b0a185b99882d2,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
5d42852b1a6dcf001785d7b6,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","One of the biggest social and practical chellenges that people living abroad face is the language barrier.Infact, every country has its own language.So, it is difficult for the person who moves to any foriegn country, because, he has to speak the foreign language.While i do admit it can be quite chellenging in first few weeks.. in my openion, most people will cover this language barrier fairely quickely.
There is no any doubt that language is the first issue for immigrants when they shifted to other countries.Initially  most of the people getting problem while talking to someone, they feel conserved  aswell because they are not that much expert in the languge used over their. Not being able to speak the native language may affect their ability to socialise and make friends.  Moreover, they have to cope up with many problems during carrier findings and job interviews.",1.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,149,76b004e7631f7335,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
69f887fe7bb8dd0012bc9d8b,"Throughout history, male leaders have led us into violence and conflict. If a society is governed by female leaders it will be more peaceful. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this opinion?","There is no dyning the fact the female leadera better than male leaders . While it is commonly hold belief that female lead better than male . 

I conclusion , in my opinion i consider that male lead better than female lead.

To begin with in big companies we see that male get succsess more than female . In other words , for there better emotional intelligent. Such as kbmg and pwx companies leaders.",0.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Government,69,aca872c42a08881c,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range|zero_band_with_substantial_text
6852d84a2969c00011221e95,"Throughout history, male leaders have led us into violence and conflict. If a society is governed by female leaders it will be more peaceful. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this opinion?","It is common knowledge that male brings about conflicts and social unrests when being appointed as leaders more than that of females. I completely agree with this opinion. This essay will discuss the opinion above.

   To begin with, men have traits that are different than that of women. Being known for bravery and boldness, men often come up with daring plans that are risky. If women are leaders, they will resolve problem in their own way so as not to put people's life in jeopardy as women are gentle and cautious. For example, 80% of researchers in Cambridge University state that women are likely to avoid confrontations or riots and often opt for safer route. Moreover, women don't like to combat as they care more about beauty and other matter.

Lastly, women are not tactical and clever like men so it is hard for them to get into big fights. They may ignore it.

   In conclusion, female leaders may bring tranquil and peace than male leaders because of their gentle characteristic and their unwillingness to get into conflict.",2.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Government,178,aca872c42a08881c,under_250_words|reported_overall_differs_from_mvp_formula|overall_outside_criterion_range
6064a763ec8b400019e3e3f1,Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems as well as practical problems . To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement ?,"Many people think that you have to speak another language if you live in an abroad nation and it has many sociological and practical issues . I totally agree with this notion because foreigners have different languages , lifestyles  , cultures and working patterns . This essay explains what are the social and practical problems which are faced by them , followed by a reasoned conclusion. 

Living in another country has some social challenges . Firstly , they feel isolated from foreign people because they have a different lifestyle than us . So Initial 6 month to one year they  face more problems during settling in other states . For instance , many Indian people migrated to Canada , Australia and America , so they have to be fluent in the English language as well as they have to adapt their culture by joining their communities , take part in social activities and so on . In the initial ,days they do not understand their importance and they confuse about it . Furthermore , they might  change eating habits that are less spicy , although nutritious  . 

Moreover , it has some practical problems like many  changes in their lifestyles . In other words , foreigners are more punctual , strict at colleges or workplace , also must obey rules and regulations of their country.  To illustrate this , they have to do more struggle to  adjust in foreign life such as use public transport because private vehicles are expensive , do part-time job as a side income , do all work on time , always talk with respects , do not make a loud noise , etc . All of these issues make their difficult life . 

To conclude , I strongly agree with this fact that living in a foreign country brings many challenges in one lifelike speak in abroad words , face many  social and practical issues.",9.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,287,76b004e7631f7335,
