5e4c01a95cd85100185e9cb6,"Some people think that newly built houses should follow the style of the old houses in the local areas, while others think that people should have freedom to build houses of their own styles. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","It is often suggested by many people to keep the infrastructure of the houses as simple as it use to be a couple of decades ago. Whereas, some believe that everyone should have a choice to choose a contemporary design for their houses. This essay will juxtapose both these views, and finally end with my opinion.

The beauty of an area can be retained if there is a symmetry among the buildings. Hence, to maintain the aesthetic beauty of a locality, it is mandatory that all new build houses and building blocks should follow the architecture of the older building. Additionally, this can also minimise the issues between the neighbours occurring due to construction. For instance, we can witness many fights in a locality because of construction of an unapproved structure of a house these days, creating an extra floor for instance, which might not be approved by the local society. These issues can be avoided if everyone follows the same housing patterns.

On the flip side, each family has a different requirement with respect to accomodation. 
For instance, a two bedroom set would be sufficient for a nucleated family, but it would not be a choice of a joint family. Therefore, giving the freedom to customise the house would be helpful to cater the needs of different kinds of families. Secondly, new architectures and constructions gives a platform to various emerging architects to showcase the talent and construct trendy and contemporary infrastructures.

In conclusion, some people this that all houses should be built with the conventional architecture to maintain the symmetry of the area and to avoid any kind of dispute due to construction. However, I feel that everyone should be given opportunity to apply their choice of architecture as it can easily cater to various requirement of different families and give to architects to show their innovation.",7.5,6.0,6.0,9.0,9.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Housing,309,1c945805324195cf,
5db4957f16286e0018e43dc3,"Living in a country where you have to speak a foreign language can cause serious social problems, as well as practical problems. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this statement?","Moving to a country where the prevailing language differs from one’s native can cause significant issues with adapting to society as well as misunderstanding on a daily basis. I strongly agree that a number of problems may arise due to language barrier. Firstly, this essay will discuss psychological aspects and an outcome of isolation from society, and secondly, it will analyze an inability to understand and correspond to simple instructions which may lead to more serious consequences. 

The primary reason why I agree with the idea that the lack of knowledge of the commonly spoken language may lead to societal disbalance is that the acceptance of the individual by society plays a crucial role in self-assurance and in basic need for communication in the life of every human being. Therefore, a person who is not being involved in the interactive process of communication is more likely to feel lonely and vulnerable as well as experience more stress and inability to share his/her negative thoughts with, at least, someone. For instance, according to recent research conducted in one of the small cities in USA close to border with Mexico figured out that immigrant who were able to speak both languages: Spanish and English were less likely to commit suicide rather then those who could only speak their mother tongue.

Another point to consider is that people who are unable to speak and understand language of the country where they stay may cause issues with fulfilling instructions or recommendations of the authorities. As a result, such a misunderstanding might cause an opportunity to fool or be unfair with the foreigner by the local population. As an example of such a situation I can think of a time when the maintenance company of the house where I am a tenant posted an announcement in Turkish stating that the monthly payment has been reduced from 2,700 Turkish Liras to 2,500 Turkish Liras. When I visited office to pay monthly rent, no one has ever mentioned a decrease in payment and charged me with the amount of 2,700 Turkish Liras. Thus, because of my inability to understand Turkish language, I was deceived and lost the money I could save.

In conclusion, I am firmly convinced that residing in a country where the majority of the population speaks another language can provoke not only challenges with assimilations in society, but may also cause troubles in a daily life constantly.",5.0,4.5,6.0,5.0,5.0,chillies/ielts-writing-task2-essays,Language,407,76b004e7631f7335,
